## 2. The Three Options Evaluated

### Option A: Set Up Other PC → Build FastAPI AI Microservice
### Option B: Harden the Node.js Server (Prepare for Microservice Integration)
### Option C: Improve Frontend/Editor Features Further

---

## 3. Detailed Analysis

### Option A — FastAPI AI Microservice on Second PC

#### What you'd do
1. Set up Docker + NVIDIA Container Toolkit on second PC
2. Create FastAPI project structure with Uvicorn
3. Build the `/process-floor-plan` endpoint
4. Set up Cloudflare Tunnels to expose it
5. Integrate an AI model (floor plan detection → JSON)

#### Dependencies & Blockers

> [!CAUTION]
> **The FastAPI service has no consumer yet.** Your Node.js server has no:
> - Queue system (BullMQ/Redis) to dispatch AI jobs
> - Job tracking table to record and update job status
> - `/api/jobs/create` endpoint to trigger processing
> - File upload flow to send floor plans to the AI service
> - Webhook/callback mechanism to receive results
>
> Building FastAPI first means you'd be building an island with no bridge to the mainland.

#### Effort: 🔴 High (2-3 weeks for a meaningful prototype)
#### Risk: 🔴 High — You'll build something you can't integrate yet
#### Value: 🟡 Medium — Core IP, but premature without the plumbing

#### Verdict
**❌ Not recommended as the immediate next step.** The AI model itself (floor plan → JSON) is your most complex R&D problem and deserves focused attention — but you'll waste time building Docker infrastructure, tunneling, and API scaffolding when your main server can't even talk to it yet. You'd also be context-switching between Python and Node.js across two machines.

---

### Option B — Harden the Node.js Server

#### What you'd do
This is about completing Phase 1 & 2 from your Backend Architecture Plan — the foundation that everything else depends on.

**Priority tasks (in dependency order):**

1. **Auth middleware** — Protect all `/api/projects` routes with JWT verification
2. **List user projects** — `GET /api/projects?userId=xxx` so the dashboard shows real data instead of mocks
3. **Delete project** — `DELETE /api/projects/:id` with ownership check
4. **Prisma schema expansion** — Add the `Scene`, `Job`, `EditorSession`, and `SubscriptionPlan` models from your architecture doc
5. **Scene endpoints** — Separate scene storage from Project (future-proof for versioning)
6. **API proxy config** — Replace hardcoded `http://localhost:5001` in the frontend with a proper proxy/env-based API URL
7. **Error handling middleware** — Centralized error handler instead of per-route try/catch
8. **Dockerize the Express server** — One `Dockerfile` + `docker-compose.yml` that runs the server with the Neon connection

#### Why this is the critical path

```
                    ┌─────────────────┐
                    │   FastAPI AI    │ ← Can't integrate without
                    │   (Option A)    │   job system in Node
                    └────────┬────────┘
                             │ needs
                    ┌────────▼────────┐
                    │  Job Tracking   │
                    │  Queue System   │
                    └────────┬────────┘
                             │ needs
                    ┌────────▼────────┐
                    │  Auth Middleware │ ← YOU ARE HERE
                    │  Project CRUD   │
                    │  Schema Models  │
                    └────────┬────────┘
                             │ needs
                    ┌────────▼────────┐
                    │  Current State  │ ✅ Done
                    │  (Basic API)    │
                    └─────────────────┘
```

Every future feature — AI processing, billing, session tracking, VR generation — depends on a properly secured, complete API with the right database models. You're one layer away from being able to plug in FastAPI.

#### Effort: 🟢 Low-Medium (1-2 weeks)
#### Risk: 🟢 Low — Incremental improvements to existing code
#### Value: 🟢 High — Unblocks everything downstream

#### Verdict
**✅ Strongly recommended.** This is the highest-leverage work you can do right now. It directly completes Phase 1 of your Backend Architecture Plan and unblocks Phase 2 and 3.

---

### Option C — Improve Frontend/Editor Features

#### What you'd do
- Add more 2D editor elements (furniture, stairs, measurements)
- Improve 3D editor (better asset browser, material picker, camera controls)
- Add responsive design fixes
- Polish UI/UX

#### Dependencies & Blockers

> [!WARNING]
> Your Master Reference Document's "Strategic Insight" section (§10) explicitly states:
> 
> *"Your moat will be: Speed, Simplicity, Reliability — Not: UI polish, Basic editor features"*
>
> Frontend features that don't plug into the pipeline (2D → AI → 3D → VR) don't move the product forward.

#### The dashboard still shows mock data
The most impactful frontend improvement would actually be connecting the dashboard to real project data — which requires Option B (list projects endpoint) first.

#### Effort: 🟡 Medium (ongoing, never "done")
#### Risk: 🟡 Medium — Risk of polishing a prototype instead of building the product
#### Value: 🔴 Low — Doesn't unblock any other work

#### Verdict
**❌ Not recommended right now.** There will always be editor improvements to make, but right now the editors are functional enough. The bottleneck is the backend, not the UI.

