## 4. Recommendation: Build Order

```
WEEK 1-2 (NOW)         WEEK 3-4              WEEK 5-6
┌──────────────┐   ┌──────────────────┐   ┌──────────────────┐
│  OPTION B    │   │  OPTION B+       │   │  OPTION A        │
│              │   │                  │   │                  │
│ • Auth MW    │──▶│ • Job model      │──▶│ • Docker FastAPI  │
│ • List/Del   │   │ • Session track  │   │ • CF Tunnels     │
│ • Schema     │   │ • File upload    │   │ • Floor plan API │
│ • Real data  │   │ • Docker Express │   │ • BullMQ queue   │
│ • API proxy  │   │ • Redis setup    │   │ • Integration    │
└──────────────┘   └──────────────────┘   └──────────────────┘
       ▲                                         │
       │                                         │
  You are here                          Then: Option C polish
```

### Specific First Sprint (This Week)

Here's exactly what I'd suggest building **on this machine, in this codebase**, before touching the second PC:

| # | Task | File(s) | Time |
|---|------|---------|------|
| 1 | Create `authMiddleware.js` — verify JWT on requests | `server/middleware/auth.js` | 1-2 hrs |
| 2 | Protect project routes with auth middleware | `server/routes/projectRoutes.js` | 30 min |
| 3 | Add `GET /api/projects` (list projects by userId from JWT) | `server/controllers/projectController.js` | 1 hr |
| 4 | Add `DELETE /api/projects/:id` with ownership check | `server/controllers/projectController.js` | 1 hr |
| 5 | Connect Dashboard to real project data (replace mock array) | `client/src/pages/Dashboard.jsx` | 2 hrs |
| 6 | Replace hardcoded `localhost:5001` with env variable | `client/src/pages/Dashboard.jsx` + `.env` | 30 min |
| 7 | Expand Prisma schema: add `Scene`, `Job`, `EditorSession` models | `server/prisma/schema.prisma` | 2 hrs |
| 8 | Run `npx prisma migrate dev` and verify | Terminal | 15 min |

**Total: ~8-10 hours of focused work → massive unlock.**

---

## 5. When to Set Up the Second PC

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Set up the second PC for FastAPI **after** you have:
> 1. ✅ Job/Scene/Session models in your Prisma schema
> 2. ✅ A `POST /api/jobs/create` endpoint in Express
> 3. ✅ Basic file upload working (even to local disk initially)
> 4. ✅ A clear contract/API spec for what the FastAPI service receives and returns
>
> At that point, spinning up FastAPI becomes a focused 2-3 day task instead of an open-ended one.

---

## 6. Summary Table

| Option | Do Now? | Effort | Risk | Unblocks | Verdict |
|--------|---------|--------|------|----------|---------|
| **A: FastAPI on 2nd PC** | ❌ | High | High | Nothing (yet) | Too early — no integration surface |
| **B: Harden Node server** | ✅ | Low-Med | Low | Everything | **Do this first** |
| **C: Editor features** | ❌ | Medium | Medium | Nothing | Polish later |

> [!TIP]
> **Bottom line**: Spend this week and next on Option B. By the end of it, your server will have auth middleware, real project listing, expanded models, and a clear API surface. *Then* set up the second PC, spin up FastAPI in Docker, and the integration will be clean and fast because the bridge already exists.
